      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mattermost): bound gateway websocket payloads at 16 MiB",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nThe Mattermost gateway websocket factory creates WebSocket connections without a maxPayload cap, relying on ws library default 100 MiB. A single oversized server frame could buffer up to 100 MiB in memory before JSON parsing.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nAdd maxPayload: 16 MiB to the Mattermost WebSocket constructor, matching the Discord gateway bound (#99998) and Signal client-container bound (#99992). 16 MiB provides generous headroom for member chunks while preventing unbounded buffering.\n\n## User Impact\nMattermost gateway websocket connections are now bounded at 16 MiB per frame, consistent with Discord and Signal channel plugins.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBefore:\n```ts\nreturn new WebSocket(url, agent ? { agent } : undefined);\n```\n\nAfter:\n```ts\nconst MATTERMOST_WS_MAX_PAYLOAD_BYTES = 16 * 1024 * 1024;\nreturn new WebSocket(url, {\n  ...(agent ? { agent } : {}),\n  maxPayload: MATTERMOST_WS_MAX_PAYLOAD_BYTES,\n});\n```\n\nExisting tests pass:\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/monitor-websocket.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  10 passed (10)\n  Duration  39.04s\n```\n\nFormatting: `npx oxfmt --check` passed. Whitespace: `git diff --check` passed.",
